{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracketSkein","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracketSkein","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Rat","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Function.Iterate","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":45,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.exists_kink_bracket_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.exists_kink_bracket_ne","kind":"theorem","line":451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L451-L471","doc":"**A genuine kink exists, and R1 genuinely fails.** In the tautological model\nover `ℚ` at `A = 2` there is a diagram `k` standing in the kink relation to the\nunknot; `bracket_kink_left` predicts `⟨k⟩ = -A⁻³ = -1/8`, which is what it is,\nand `-1/8 ≠ 1 = ⟨unknot⟩`.\n\nThis is the non-vacuity witness for `bracket_kink_left`, and it is also the\nconcrete reason the bracket specified here is *not* a link invariant: the writhe\ncorrection is exactly what repairs this failure, and it is not formalised in this\nfile. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.exists_bracket_addCircle_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.exists_bracket_addCircle_ne","kind":"theorem","line":440,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L440-L449","doc":"**The model is non-degenerate**: over `ℚ` at `A = 2` the bracket is not\nconstant, since `⟨unknot ⊔ circle⟩ = δ = -17/4 ≠ 1 = ⟨unknot⟩`. So the theorems\nabove are not statements about a collapsed model in which every diagram has the\nsame bracket. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.tautological_smoothing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.tautological_smoothing","kind":"theorem","line":433,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L433-L438","doc":"**The smoothing relation of the tautological model is inhabited**, for every\npair `(y, z)`. This matters: a specification whose `Smoothing` relation were\nempty would satisfy K1 vacuously, and every theorem above that takes a\n`Smoothing` hypothesis would be contentless. It is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.tautological","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.tautological","kind":"def","line":416,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L416-L431","doc":"The **tautological model**: take the diagram type to be `R` itself, with the\nbracket the identity. Every one of K1, K2, K3 holds, the last two by `rfl`.\n\nThis model exists for every commutative ring `R` and every pair `A`, `Ainv` with\n`A * Ainv = 1`, so the specification is consistent in complete generality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.unreduced_unlink","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.unreduced_unlink","kind":"theorem","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L400-L406","doc":"The `(n+1)`-component unlink has unreduced bracket `δⁿ⁺¹` — one factor of\n`δ` per component — against `δⁿ` for the reduced bracket of `bracket_unlink`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.unreduced_unknot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.unreduced_unknot","kind":"theorem","line":395,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L395-L398","doc":"**The reduced/unreduced relationship at the unknot**: the normalisation K3 is\nwhere the two conventions differ, and they differ by exactly one factor of `δ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.unreduced_loop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.unreduced_loop","kind":"theorem","line":390,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L390-L393","doc":"The unreduced bracket obeys the same loop rule K2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.unreduced_skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.unreduced_skein","kind":"theorem","line":385,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L385-L388","doc":"The unreduced bracket obeys the same skein rule K1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.unreduced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.unreduced","kind":"def","line":382,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L382-L383","doc":"The **unreduced bracket** `δ · ⟨-⟩`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.scale_eq_one_of_normalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.scale_eq_one_of_normalised","kind":"theorem","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L362-L374","doc":"K3 is exactly what pins the scale: the only rescaling of a normalised\nbracket that is again normalised is the identity. Read with `smul_skein` and\n`smul_loop`: rescaling carries solutions of K1–K2 to solutions, so K1 and K2\nnever pin a bracket by themselves, and K3 picks out `c = 1` within each such\nrescaling family.\n\nThis does **not** say that any two solutions of K1–K2 differ by a scalar, which\nis false. Take `Smoothing` empty, so that K1 holds vacuously, and `D := R × R`\nwith `addCircle := (δ • ·)`; both coordinate projections satisfy K2, and they are\nnot scalar multiples of one another. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.smul_loop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.smul_loop","kind":"theorem","line":357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L357-L360","doc":"K2 is **homogeneous** as well. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.smul_skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.smul_skein","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L351-L355","doc":"K1 is **homogeneous**: rescaling the bracket by any `c : R` preserves the\nskein rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_kink_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_kink_pair","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L339-L345","doc":"One kink followed by the opposite kink restores the bracket. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.kinkFactor_mul_kinkFactor_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.kinkFactor_mul_kinkFactor_inv","kind":"theorem","line":328,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L328-L335","doc":"The two kink factors are mutually inverse. This is the algebraic fact\nunderlying the well-definedness of the writhe correction `(-A³)^{-w}`: cancelling\none kink against the opposite one returns the original bracket. The correction\nitself is *not* formalised here — it needs a writhe, hence an oriented diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_kink_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_kink_right","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L317-L324","doc":"**Kink with the circle on the `A`-smoothing.** With the two smoothings\nexchanged, `⟨k⟩ = -A³ ⟨d⟩`. This is the factor the usual convention attaches to a\n*positive* curl — but, as in `bracket_kink_left`, nothing here fixes that\nassignment, because there is no writhe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_kink_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_kink_left","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L305-L315","doc":"**Kink with the circle on the `B`-smoothing.** If `k` is a crossing whose\n`A`-smoothing is `d` and whose `B`-smoothing is `d` with a trivial circle\nadjoined, then `⟨k⟩ = -A⁻³ ⟨d⟩`.\n\nDeliberately *not* called the positive curl: signing a curl requires an\norientation and a writhe, and `D` carries neither. On the usual convention it is\nthe other case, `bracket_kink_right`, that is the positive one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_sub_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_sub_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L292-L297","doc":"The difference form of `bracket_add_mirror`:\n`⟨d⟩ - ⟨d'⟩ = (A - A⁻¹)(⟨d₀⟩ - ⟨d₁⟩)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_add_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_add_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L285-L290","doc":"A crossing and its **mirror** (the same smoothing pair, in the opposite\norder) satisfy `⟨d⟩ + ⟨d'⟩ = (A + A⁻¹)(⟨d₀⟩ + ⟨d₁⟩)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_eq_of_smoothing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_eq_of_smoothing","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L278-L283","doc":"The bracket of a crossing is **determined** by the brackets of its two\nsmoothings: two diagrams with the same smoothing pair have the same bracket. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_unlink","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_unlink","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L268-L272","doc":"**The unlink.** The diagram obtained from the unknot by adjoining `n` trivial\ncircles — that is, the `(n+1)`-component unlink — has bracket `δⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_iterate_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_iterate_add","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L262-L266","doc":"Circle counts add: `m` circles on top of `n` circles is `m + n` circles. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_iterate_addCircle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_iterate_addCircle","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L253-L260","doc":"**Adding `n` disjoint trivial circles multiplies the bracket by `δⁿ`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.δ_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.δ_sq","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L247-L249","doc":"`δ² = A⁴ + 2 + A⁻⁴`, for a specification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.A_sq_mul_δ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.A_sq_mul_δ","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L243-L245","doc":"The defining quadratic of the loop value, for a specification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_addCircle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket_addCircle","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L237-L241","doc":"K2 restated in terms of `S.δ`. This is a notational restatement, true by\nunfolding `δ`; the mathematical content is the structure field `loop`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.δ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.δ","kind":"def","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L234-L235","doc":"The loop value of a specification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.normalisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.normalisation","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L228-L228","doc":"**K3, the normalisation.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.loop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.loop","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L226-L226","doc":"**K2, the loop rule**, with loop value `δ = -(A² + A⁻²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.skein","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L223-L223","doc":"**K1, the bracket skein rule.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.Smoothing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.Smoothing","kind":"def","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L221-L221","doc":"`Smoothing d d₀ d₁`: `d` carries a distinguished crossing whose\n`A`-smoothing is `d₀` and whose `B`-smoothing is `d₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.addCircle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.addCircle","kind":"def","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L218-L218","doc":"Adjoin a disjoint trivial circle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.unknot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.unknot","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L216-L216","doc":"The distinguished one-component trivial diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.bracket","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L214-L214","doc":"The bracket itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.A_mul_Ainv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.A_mul_Ainv","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L212-L212","doc":"`Ainv` really is a two-sided inverse of `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.Ainv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.Ainv","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L210-L210","doc":"A stand-in for `A⁻¹`, kept as a separate scalar so that `R` need only be a\n`CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.A","kind":"def","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L207-L207","doc":"The bracket variable `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec.mk","kind":"ctor","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L205-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.KauffmanBracketSpec","kind":"structure","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L197-L228","doc":"A **Kauffman bracket specification** on a type `D` of diagrams, valued in a\ncommutative ring `R`.\n\nThe three fields `skein`, `loop` and `normalisation` are Kauffman's rules K1, K2\nand K3. `D` is opaque and `Smoothing` is an abstract ternary relation: this\nstructure encodes the *algebra* of the bracket and contains no diagram\ncombinatorics whatsoever. See the module docstring on what is and is not\nclaimed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.loopValue_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.loopValue_sq","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L188-L193","doc":"The square of the loop value, `δ² = A⁴ + 2 + A⁻⁴`. The middle `2` is where\n`A * Ainv = 1` is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.Ainv_sq_mul_loopValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.Ainv_sq_mul_loopValue","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L182-L186","doc":"The mirror form of `A_sq_mul_loopValue`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.A_sq_mul_loopValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.A_sq_mul_loopValue","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L174-L180","doc":"**The defining quadratic of the loop value.** `δ` satisfies\n`A²·δ + A⁴ + 1 = 0`; equivalently `δ = -(A⁴ + 1)/A²`. This is a genuine\nconsequence of `A * Ainv = 1` — it is false for unconstrained `Ainv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.cube_mul_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.cube_mul_cube","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L170-L172","doc":"From `A * A⁻¹ = 1`, the cubes are inverse too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.sq_mul_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.sq_mul_sq","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L166-L168","doc":"From `A * A⁻¹ = 1`, the squares are inverse too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.loopValue_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.loopValue_symm","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L158-L162","doc":"The loop value is symmetric under the swap `A ↔ A⁻¹` — the substitution that\nmirroring induces on the bracket variable. (Mirroring itself is not defined here;\n`D` carries no structure.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.loopValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.KauffmanBracket.loopValue","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/KauffmanBracketSkein.lean#L154-L156","doc":"The **loop value** `δ = -(A² + A⁻²)` of the Kauffman bracket, written with an\nexplicit stand-in `Ainv` for `A⁻¹` so that the base ring stays a `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}